How do we find the box number?

This is the important formula:
int box = (row / 3) * 3 + (col / 3);

The Sudoku boxes are numbered:
┌─────────┬─────────┬─────────┐
│    0    │    1    │    2    │
├─────────┼─────────┼─────────┤
│    3    │    4    │    5    │
├─────────┼─────────┼─────────┤
│    6    │    7    │    8    │
└─────────┴─────────┴─────────┘


Suppose:

row = 4
col = 7

Then:
(row / 3) * 3 + (col / 3)

= (4 / 3) * 3 + (7 / 3)
= 1 * 3 + 2
= 5

So (4,7) belongs to box 5.

If we put 5 there:

boxes[5][5] = true;


Meaning:

Box 5 already contains number 5.

Later, if we try to put another 5 anywhere inside that same 3×3 box:

if (boxes[5][5])
    return false;

Immediately invalid.




class Sudoku {

    private int[][] board = new int[9][9];

    // rows[row][num] = whether num already exists in that row
    private boolean[][] rows = new boolean[9][10];

    // cols[col][num] = whether num already exists in that column
    private boolean[][] cols = new boolean[9][10];

    // boxes[box][num] = whether num already exists in that 3x3 box
    private boolean[][] boxes = new boolean[9][10];

    public boolean placeNumber(int row, int col, int num) {

        if (board[row][col] != 0)
            return false;

        int box = (row / 3) * 3 + (col / 3);

        // Already present?
        if (rows[row][num] ||
            cols[col][num] ||
            boxes[box][num]) {
            return false;
        }

        // Place number
        board[row][col] = num;

        rows[row][num] = true;
        cols[col][num] = true;
        boxes[box][num] = true;

        return true;
    }
}
